  "name": "D1: war/peace chain — declare, offer, accept, break",
  "notes": "A105: the pair has MET (the engine now refuses diplomacy with a civ you have not met) and therefore already carries the EXPLICIT war entry contactPass writes at first contact — so the opening declare is refused as alreadyWar rather than accepted, and WAR_DECLARED is in practice a TREATY-BREAK event. Chain: declare (refused, war already explicit) -> offer timed peace -> p2 accepts (PEACE_TREATY_SIGNED, expiresTurn) -> p1 breaks it (TREATY_BROKEN + reputation+ toward Treacherous, D5). Pins the relations entry + the D5 reputation band (0..repMax) cross-language.",
